From ccb8f1067c55495d1813693ab1a750ac52e42ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:19:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: Phone tab becomes Bluetooth, with "add device" for
 OBD adapters and tire sensors

The tab is now "Bluetooth". Besides "pair new phone" (the unit becomes
visible and the phone pairs), "add device" makes the unit look for devices
itself for 60 s, classic and LE, and lists them under "Nearby devices" as
OBD-II adapters (by name: OBD, ELM327, V-LINK, Vgate, Veepeak, ...), tire
sensors (company 0x0100 adverts, what ozark-vehicled decodes), phones and
other devices.

- OBD adapters and other devices pair from here. Legacy devices asking
  for a PIN get 1234 then 0000 (OBD adapters) or 0000 then 1234, retried
  on an authentication failure. A paired OBD adapter becomes the vehicle
  service's adapter (obd_link elm327-bt, obd_bt_address); in the paired
  list it shows "used for the vehicle" or a "use for OBD" button
  instead of connect/disconnect, since the vehicle service opens it.
- Tire sensors only broadcast, so they aren't paired: "set wheel" puts
  one on a wheel (AssignTpmsSensor) and turns Bluetooth tire sensors on.

Paired devices get an icon by kind. Settings > Vehicle points at the
Bluetooth tab for pairing an OBD adapter.
